description:
Langan provides expert land development engineering and environmental consulting services for major developers, renewable energy producers, energy companies, corporations, healthcare systems, colleges/universities, and large infrastructure programs throughout the U.S. and around the world. Our employees collaborate seamlessly among 50+ offices and gain valuable hands-on experience that fosters career growth. Langan culture is entrepreneurial from advancing innovative technical solutions, to participating in robust training and knowledge sharing, to making progressive change within the communities we live and work.

Consistently ranked among the top ten “Best Firms to Work For” and Engineering News-Record’s top 50 firms worldwide, Langan attracts and retains the best talent in the industry. Employees thrive at Langan, a firm that fosters an inclusive and supportive work environment for all; prioritizes wellbeing, health, and safety; encourages volunteerism and philanthropy; offers workplace flexibility, along with carbon-neutral office spaces; and empowers individuals to contribute their skills and knowledge to make impactful contributions.
Job Summary

Langan is seeking an Environmental Data Analyst to join its collaborative team in New York City. This individual will serve a key function in providing technical support to field sampling teams, the collection of and configuration of large datasets and the development of and utilization of data validation tools to identify quality issues. In this role, you will have the opportunity to partner cross-functionally as part of a growing national team.

Job Responsibilities
• Assist with organizing, reviewing, and managing environmental analytical and field data for investigation and remediation projects;
• Support the preparation of tables, figures, and summaries for technical reports, client deliverables, and regulatory submissions;
• Work with enterprise databases and tools such as EarthSoft EQuIS, Excel, and Power BI to identify and resolve data quality issues;
• Coordinate with project teams, laboratories, data validators, and GIS staff to ensure complete and accurate datasets;
• Track and apply regulatory criteria and environmental standards (state and federal) under guidance of senior staff;
• Participate in the development and improvement of data management workflows and internal tools;
• Maintain strong attention to detail while learning industry best practices for environmental data QA/QC;
• Track and apply regulatory criteria and environmental standards (state and federal) under guidance of senior staff; and,
• Participate in the development and improvement of data management workflows and internal tools.Stay current with emerging industry standards and technologies related to environmental data management.

Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree in environmental science, geology, engineering, data science, computer science, or a related field;
• 0–3 years of experience in environmental data management, environmental consulting, or a related analytical role;
• Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel; exposure to databases or data tools (EQuIS, SQL, Power BI) is a plus; and,
• Familiarity with environmental sampling data, laboratory deliverables, or regulatory reporting is a plus.

Langan provides a rich array of programs and benefits to help its employees advance their careers and enhance the quality of their lives. Our comprehensive compensation package includes: full-time employment company paid medical, dental, and vision coverage; life insurance, short- and long-term disability insurance, and paid pregnancy disability leave; 401(k)/Roth with company match; paid time off including parental and military leave; employee referral and professional license bonuses; and educational reimbursement.

Langan offers employee resource groups; flexible work schedules; extensive training; wellness programs; buddy and mentoring programs; and much more!

Langan is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants and employees, including individuals with disabilities and protected veterans. We believe that an inclusive workplace is essential for the well-being and success of our employees.

Certain US jurisdictions require Langan to include an estimate of salary or hourly ranges. The estimated range for this role is: $65,000 - $88,500. Actual compensation may vary based on factors such as related work experience, location, market conditions, education/training, certifications and other credentials, as well as applicable knowledge and skills. Certain roles may be eligible for overtime and participation in the firm's annual bonus and performance review program. Bonuses are discretionary and based on individual job performance and the profitability of the firm. Employees are also eligible to receive up to 20 days of paid vacation time, 10 days of paid sick time and 10 paid holidays throughout the year. Eligibility and actual paid time off may vary based on local law and factors such as hours worked, related work experience and level.

Job Summary

The primary purpose of this position is to physically unpack valuable packages, verify documentation, inspect contents, tag, loop and enter attributes in the GEM system.

Key Duties, Responsibilities and Accountabilities
• Receive valuable packages and ensure the documentation for each shipment and the physical items match;
• Open and inspect job bags, ensure there’s no empty flutes, weigh each piece and record information on vendor’s invoice, verify GIA Certs have been added to GEM, verify stock # stamp against paperwork and GEM, check Bill of Materials (quantity, metal fineness) in the GEM system, tag each piece, print and affix label to tags;
• Ensure the accuracy of merchandise received as well as moved out to QA and GA;
• Systematically record all incoming merchandise and reconcile against shipments;
• Handle and pack all jewelry and components for internal movement (place pieces into membrane boxes or wrap items in trans-wrap/pink bags, place internal package into a clear plastic job bag and apply coloured code identifier to outside of bag by product type);
• Transfer job bags to GA WIP or QA WIP;
• Verify circulating stock to assure the tag corresponds the product;
• Match circulating stock to stock number and item description in Gem;
• Control the outflow of goods to meet regular scheduled processing times;
• Identify exceptions to standard process flow movement to improve team efficiencies;
• Report merchandise movement activity;
• Maintain movement records;
• Monitor packing supplies, request additional supplies as necessary with internal teams;
• Perform monthly physical inventory to ensure accountability of all merchandise in the receiving area; research and resolve any discrepancies;
• Enforce company-wide compliance, in accordance with applicable policies and procedures relating to property movement, working and storing of merchandise; and
• Perform additional administrative duties as necessary.

Job Qualifications
• 2 years related work experience, luxury retail preferred;
• Bachelor’s degree;
• Strong organizational skills to manage inventory and associated documentation and materials;
• Must be team oriented and able to create strong relationships with all cross-functional teams;
• Proficient computer skills required, MS Office applications (Outlook, Excel);
• Graduate Gemologist, gemstone, jewelry and vault knowledge a plus.
